body:
`view <module>` lists an outline but not the module comment or imports. `read` refuses a source file held as symbols, and `view <module> --bodies` dumps the whole file, so learning a module's imports can cost a large read. In task:21241abf8e6ac8a7 the worker needed three turns to discover a moved test file's header this way.

Show a module's comment and imports in `view <module>`, or add `view <module> --header` or `--imports`. Keep `--bodies` behavior unchanged, and do not dump function bodies just to show the header.

Tests:
- a module with a comment and imports shows both without its bodies;
- an ordinary outline is unchanged;
- a missing module still reports an unknown name.
